      "value": "Address-decoded 128KB SRAM macro composed of four 32KB banks with muxed read data output.",
      "explanation": "The module has a 14-bit address input (i_addr_14) and four chip-select decode assignments (csb_0 through csb_3) that select one of four banks based on address bits [13:12]. The 64-bit read data output (o_data_64) is muxed from four internal 64-bit data buses (w_data_64_s0 through w_data_64_s3) using the same address bits. No event inputs, event outputs, control inputs, or reset port are present, indicating a purely combinatorial read path with no clocked control logic.",
      "certainty": "ai_inferred",
      "confidence": "high",
